# NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 NVLink-5 scale-up domain: 72 GPUs, one non-blocking NVSwitch hop.
# Sources, bandwidth convention, and abstraction caveats: see README.md in this folder.
# Comments below explain only the values in this file.
#
# Nodes 72             72 Blackwell GPUs (the NVLink endpoints).
# Tiers 2, Podsize 72  One physical NVSwitch stage; htsim rejects Tiers=1, so this is a
#                      degenerate 2-tier fat-tree: Podsize==Nodes and Tier-0 Radix_Down==Nodes
#                      put all 72 GPUs on ONE ToR, and Tier-1 is vestigial.
# Downlink_speed_Gbps  7200 = per-host unidirectional rate (1800 GB/s bidir x 4).
# Radix_Down 72        all 72 GPUs attach to the single ToR.
# Radix_Up 1 +         one vestigial uplink; the parser requires Radix_Down/Radix_Up ==
#   Oversubscribed 72  Oversubscribed (72/1 == 72). It carries no host<->host traffic, so the
#                      host tier is 1:1 non-blocking (NOT 72:1 oversubscribed).
# Tier-1 Radix_Down 1  the vestigial spine (unused; present only to satisfy Tiers >= 2).
# Latency 100 / 30 ns  Switch_Latency_ns / Downlink_Latency_ns are ESTIMATES (NVIDIA discloses
#                      no NVSwitch latency). ToR port count = 72 + 1 = 73 <= htsim's 96-port cap.
Nodes 72
Tiers 2
Podsize 72

Tier 0
Downlink_speed_Gbps 7200
Radix_Down 72
Radix_Up 1
Downlink_Latency_ns 30
Switch_Latency_ns 100
Oversubscribed 72

Tier 1
Downlink_speed_Gbps 7200
Radix_Down 1
Downlink_Latency_ns 30
Switch_Latency_ns 100
